    {
      "id": "frame-state-snapshot-and-reset-serialization-gap",
      "category": "conditional_concurrency_risk",
      "severity": "MEDIUM_FUNCTIONAL_CONSISTENCY",
      "disposition": "INHERITED_FROM_STOCK; STATIC_INTERLEAVING_PLAUSIBLE; NO_MEMORY_SAFETY_FAILURE_PROVEN",
      "details": "syna_ioctl snapshots tcm+0x438 and tcm+0x5e0 before acquiring frame_mutex at +0x470. The report callback registered for entity 17 reads +0x5e0 and, when enabled, copies up to 204800 bytes into the frame buffer at +0x460 and updates +0x438/+0x468 without that mutex. tpd_set_frame_data writes +0x5e0 before calling zte_reset_frame_list, which uses +0x470 while clearing frame metadata and the buffer; syna_dev_suspend also clears +0x5e0 without +0x470. Thus the lock in syna_ioctl does not serialize the snapshot with these accesses, and reset can interleave with frame production if the callback and control path overlap. The copy length is capped at the 204800-byte probe allocation, so this evidence does not establish an out-of-bounds write or use-after-free. Runtime scheduling and teardown interleavings were not reproduced.",
      "evidence": {
        "frame_mutex_probe_init": "syna_dev_probe.c initializes +0x470 before misc_register",
        "report_callback_registration": "syna_dev_set_up_input_device.c registers syna_dev_process_touch_report for report/entity 17",
